Subject: [qnx-porter 0002] bool-typedef
Source: deterministic rule
Reason: src/MQTTPacket.h defines its own `bool`, but on QNX 8.0 <sys/socket.h> already includes <stdbool.h> (via io-sock/types_fbsd.h), so `bool` is taken. The typedef is skipped when stdbool's bool is visible. Note: bool is then _Bool, not unsigned int, in those files.
Error: /home/chirag/qnx-porter/ports/paho.mqtt.c/work/src/src/MQTTPacket.h:31:22: error: two or more data types in declaration specifiers
---
diff --git a/src/MQTTPacket.h b/src/MQTTPacket.h
index fd384ae..ecdae83 100644
--- a/src/MQTTPacket.h
+++ b/src/MQTTPacket.h
@@ -28,7 +28,9 @@
 #include "LinkedList.h"
 #include "Clients.h"
 
+#ifndef __bool_true_false_are_defined  /* qnx-porter: QNX's <sys/socket.h> includes <stdbool.h> */
 typedef unsigned int bool;
+#endif
 typedef void* (*pf)(int, unsigned char, char*, size_t);
 
 #include "MQTTProperties.h"
